    (OUT/'report.tex').write_text(preamble+'\n'.join(doc.tex)+'\n\\end{document}\n')
    (OUT/'report.md').write_text('\n'.join(doc.md))
    (OUT/'methodology_audit.md').write_text('# Methodology and data-integrity audit\n\n'+method_text+'\n\n'+
        '## Integrity and provenance\n\nAll 310 structural checks passed. See `tables/audit_checks.csv`, `tables/campaign_audit.csv`, `tables/perf_audit.csv` and the complete source/data hash inventories. The 17,600 physical measurements comprise 11,200 eligible and 6,400 obsolete measurements. No corrupt, failed, missing or duplicate measurement was removed. All eight perf events report 100% running; exit 130 is deliberate SIGINT. The cached dataset and current binary match every recorded hash. Both repositories were marked dirty at collection; present tracked source matches recorded revisions, but historical uncommitted state was not archived. Intended build: release, target-cpu=native; exact build environment and continuous host state are not archived.\n\n'+
        '## Long acquisition gaps\n\n'+gaps.to_markdown(index=False)+'\n\nThese gaps interrupt blocks, not just campaign boundaries. Main results retain them; `interruption_sensitivity.csv` removes each affected block (19 remaining) without modifying any raw data. The gap cause is unknown. This qualifies the assumption of locally comparable randomized blocks.\n\n'+
        '## Reproduction and preservation\n\nRun `python analysis/bls_full/run.py` with dependencies in `requirements.txt`. The pipeline never invokes the benchmark, compiles Rust, writes to SQLite, or edits the completed campaigns. SQLite uses mode=ro and immutable=1. `input_inventory.csv` fingerprints all original artifacts and cached datasets; `validation.json` records the final comparison.\n')
    (OUT/'statistical_diagnostics.md').write_text('# Statistical diagnostics and sensitivity\n\n'+diag_text+'\n\n## Statistical settings\n\n```json\n'+json.dumps(settings,indent=2)+'\n```\n\nEvery raw observation remains in the main results. Supplemental CSV tables retain non-significant tests and all sensitivity estimates, including unfavorable findings.\n')
    command=['xelatex']
    format_dir=None
    if not subprocess.run(['kpsewhich','xelatex.fmt'],capture_output=True,text=True).stdout.strip():
        # Some TeX installations ship the engine and sources but omit the XeLaTeX format.
        # Build it in /tmp, never in a system or user configuration directory.
        format_dir=tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix='bls-tex-')
        ini=subprocess.check_output(['kpsewhich','xelatex.ini'],text=True).strip()
        built=subprocess.run(['xetex','-ini','-etex','-jobname=xelatex','-progname=xelatex',ini],cwd=format_dir.name,capture_output=True,text=True)
        if built.returncode:raise RuntimeError(built.stdout[-4000:])
        command+=['-fmt='+str(Path(format_dir.name)/'xelatex.fmt')]
    for run in range(2):
        result=subprocess.run(command+['-interaction=nonstopmode','-halt-on-error','report.tex'],cwd=OUT,stdout=subprocess.PIPE,stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,text=True)
        (OUT/f'latex_pass_{run+1}.log').write_text(result.stdout)
        if result.returncode:raise RuntimeError(result.stdout[-5000:])
    if format_dir:format_dir.cleanup()
    print('PDF report compiled',flush=True)

